It returns an `*echo.HTTPError` with status 500 built from the pooled value asserted to `error` (middleware/decompress.go:93-97):

```go
i := pool.Get()
gr, ok := i.(*gzip.Reader)
if !ok {
    return echo.NewHTTPError(http.StatusInternalServerError, i.(error).Error())
}
```

So the response is 500 Internal Server Error whose message is `i.(error).Error()` — the pool's `New` func returns an `error` when `gzip.NewWriterLevel`/`gzip.NewReader` fails, and that is what gets reported. (Note the second assertion is unchecked: if the pooled value is neither a `*gzip.Reader` nor an `error`, this panics.)
